From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:25:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lips): repair single-frame landmark glitches before
 LatentSync; guard patch spikes; ASR length cap and tail recovery

- Fast hand motion gave 1-2 frames of wrong landmarks (18.8 s of the test clip); they drove
  both the face alignment and the mouth envelope, pasting a twisted, oversized mouth. Frames
  that jump in position/size against their neighbours are now re-estimated from good frames.
- Compositor keeps the source mouth for a frame whose generated area suddenly exceeds 2.5x the
  recent median (a misplaced patch rather than speech).
- Merging short ASR pieces can no longer exceed the 9 s sentence cap; when word mode stops
  early, the missing tail is taken from the segment-mode pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
